@lesson dart-m05-l02 | Sets | 10
## Learning objectives
- Store unique values with `Set`
- Use set operations: union, intersection, difference
- Know when a set is better than a list

## Unique, unordered-by-meaning values
A `Set` holds **unique** elements. Adding a duplicate has no effect. Dart's default `Set` is a `LinkedHashSet`, which preserves insertion order when iterating.

```dart
void main() {
  final tags = <String>{'dart', 'flutter'};
  tags.add('dart');        // ignored, already present
  tags.add('firebase');
  print(tags);             // {dart, flutter, firebase}
  print(tags.length);      // 3
  print(tags.contains('flutter')); // true
}
```

> WARNING: `{}` on its own creates an empty **Map**, not a Set. Write `<String>{}` or `Set<String>()` for an empty set.

## Set operations
```dart
void main() {
  final alice = {'dart', 'go', 'rust'};
  final bob = {'dart', 'kotlin', 'go'};

  print(alice.union(bob));        // {dart, go, rust, kotlin}
  print(alice.intersection(bob)); // {dart, go}
  print(alice.difference(bob));   // {rust}
}
```

## Fast lookups
`contains` on a set is typically constant time, whereas on a list it scans every element. For large collections where you frequently ask "is this in here?", a set is much faster.

```dart
void main() {
  final completedLessons = {'dart-m01-l01', 'dart-m01-l02'};
  bool isDone(String id) => completedLessons.contains(id);
  print(isDone('dart-m01-l02')); // true
}
```

This is exactly how Bimo checks which lessons you've completed.

## Removing duplicates
```dart
final emails = ['a@x.com', 'b@x.com', 'a@x.com'];
final unique = emails.toSet().toList(); // [a@x.com, b@x.com]
```

## Equality matters
Sets use `==` and `hashCode` to detect duplicates. Two instances of your own class are considered different unless you override both (Module 6).

:::check What does `{1, 2, 2, 3}.length` return?
3. Duplicates are not stored.
:::

## Common mistakes
- Writing `var s = {};` and getting a `Map<dynamic, dynamic>`.
- Expecting index access: sets have no `[]` operator; use `elementAt` or convert to a list.

## Summary
- Sets store unique elements and keep insertion order (LinkedHashSet).
- `union`, `intersection`, `difference` combine sets.
- `contains` is fast; use sets for membership checks and deduplication.

## Further learning
- api.dart.dev ▸ dart:core ▸ Set
